{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review overlap detector flagged 1909-c1a7-9f20-440f (brattish-ladyish-jaguar, closed) at 0.72 on shared artifact _build-and-test.yml. Reviewed: NOT a duplicate. 1909 is the same defect CLASS (definition-vs-tree skew: the Verified lane runs the workflow definition from trusted main against the patchset tree) but a different mechanism — it guarded gate steps that invoke a repo SCRIPT absent from a stale tree, and added a structural guard scoped to script-running steps. This bug is the pytest-marker-selection variant (macOS selects -m platform_compat, a marker applied only by the current-tree conftest), which 1909's script-oriented guard correctly does not cover. Independent reproduction, distinct fix site. Recording as same-class sibling, not linking duplicates (which would corrupt escape metrics)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787719756309230001,"uuid":"6bc1f6ce-7ce2-438c-8e8c-4c65fca875b6"}